 own 5% or more of our common stock, together with their affiliates and related persons, in aggregate, owned approximately 43.8% of our outstanding common stock as of December 31, 2025. Our directors and executive officers together with their respective affiliates owned, in the aggregate, approximately 31.7% of our outstanding common stock as of December 31, 2025. Our principal stockholders, if acting together (with or without our directors and executive officers), may have the ability to exert substantial influence over the outcome of matters submitted to our stockholders for approval, including the election and removal of directors and any merger or sale of all or substantially all of our assets. In addition, our principal stockholders, if acting together (with or without our directors and executive officers), may have the ability to exert substantial influence over the management and affairs of our company. Accordingly, this concentration of ownership could harm the market price of our common stock by:","context":"Our principal stockholders, in aggregate, could exert substantial influence over us which could delay or prevent a change in corporate control or result in the entrenchment of management or the board of directors.","section":"•period-to-period fluctuations in our financial condition and results of operations, including the timing of receipt of any milestone or other payments under commercialization or licensing agreements;","block":916,"table":null,"attribution":"management","interpretation":"source_excerpt_not_independently_verified","source":{"accession":"0001937653-26-000015","form":"10-K","filedAt":"2026-03-02","reportDate":"2025-12-31","cik":"0001937653","url":"https://www.sec.gov/Archives/edgar/data/1937653/000193765326000015/zyme-20251231.htm","rawPath":"sec/raw/152a5ca69a0b87ace643468f02589a23eec2a2a5ffb64fa93beb0028842129df.bin","sha256":"152a5ca69a0b87ace643468f02589a23eec2a2a5ffb64fa93beb0028842129df"}},{"id":"9154e8505a5dfe300294fe077e8fb70e